Track 2: "Who Cleared the Twelve o’Clock Ledger?"
- Story & Context: Maeve Higgins arrived three hours late for her initial recording session at the abbey gatehouse, carrying only a pair of battered Paiste hi-hats and smelling unmistakably of damp raincoats and menthol tobacco. She found Brother Kilian trembling by the four-track tape machine, frantically confessing that his dream-transcription patch had accidentally generated an irrepressibly bouncy, sunny chord progression instead of a somber midday prayer. Smirking at his panic, Maeve slammed her cymbals onto an unpadded stand and kicked a sluggish Bristol trip-hop groove straight through his runaway arpeggios, shouting into the room mic: "We missed the appointment, honey, so keep the tambourine spinning!" The resulting jam erased Kilian's liturgical guilt in under five minutes, capturing the definitive, laughing character piece of the genre's earliest days.
