Track 3: Uhrwerk-Rausch
- Story & Context: By midsummer 1996, the annual meadow gathering behind the abbey had turned into an unsanctioned five-hundred-person celebration where dancers kicked up clouds of pollen beneath the afternoon sun. When municipal bailiffs finally arrived clutching clipboards to issue missed-curfew citations, their papers were swept away in a deafening stampede of swinging sub-bass and clattering bronze cymbals. The session peaked when the monastery's central turret clock mechanism jammed on its hourly chime, triggering fifty patch-cables to spit a joyous major-seventh fanfare as the crowd roared the refrain: "Nobody knows the hour, so we build the chapel here!" The myth of that unpoliced, golden afternoon cemented the subculture, proving that mechanical time could be permanently conquered by ecstatic rhythm.
